1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:07,410
One scheduled instant. Two reports in the database.

2
00:00:07,410 --> 00:00:10,820
The application committed both.

3
00:00:10,820 --> 00:00:15,710
Two processes, two connections, one database.

4
00:00:15,710 --> 00:00:23,850
Both checks say absent. The barrier releases both. Both commit.

5
00:00:23,850 --> 00:00:33,170
Unique key on report type + scheduled UTC instant.

6
00:00:33,170 --> 00:00:41,460
Zero changes: verify. Busy: retry. Other constraint: error.

7
00:00:41,460 --> 00:00:46,250
Same stale check, same barrier, same release.

8
00:00:46,250 --> 00:00:51,730
Only one connection can hold the write lock.

9
00:00:51,730 --> 00:00:57,740
One worker commits the complete report.

10
00:00:57,740 --> 00:01:05,760
The other detects it and exits. One row.

11
00:01:05,760 --> 00:01:12,470
Controlled fault: killed after insert, before commit.

12
00:01:12,470 --> 00:01:17,270
Another connection sees zero rows.

13
00:01:17,270 --> 00:01:25,100
Rollback: zero rows. Retry: exactly one report.

14
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:30,690
Busy is retryable, not completed.

15
00:01:30,690 --> 00:01:37,620
One committed report per logical run. Not exactly-once.

16
00:01:37,620 --> 00:01:43,680
Scheduling starts work. Coordination decides what commits.
